      "anchor": "P1 registration enables P2 requests, but N1 remains dashboard-pending through boundary 3 after recognition. Bulk selection can spend scarce FIFO delivery ticks on duplicates.",
      "burden": "Transfer ledger: registration clerk performs six validations; dispatcher spends six request actions and owns timing, identity selection and tick-3 restraint. Record each boundary, chosen control, targets, queue entries, recognition, duplicates and failures. R6 readings add zero stipulated clerk labor; they do not make choices. Trial bookkeeping and later maintenance effort are unknown. Server retains one delivery per tick.",
      "construction": "Migrate selection timing into readable R6 ledgers and delivery commitments into R5 queue. Validate N3,N4,N5,N6,N7,N8 at ticks 0,1,2,3,4,5. Request individual N2,N3,N4 at 0,1,2; idle at 3; bulk N5,N6 at 4; individual N7 at 5 and N8 at 6.",
      "defeat": "Any illegal request, seventh dispatcher action, ledger disagreement, or fewer than eight registrations or recognitions defeats the success claim. Attack success would refute the claimed necessity of this manual boundary restraint.",
